      "mechanism": "ascii_tree_continuous_reward (weight 0.7) uses only the longest matching block, max(matcher.get_matching_blocks(), key=size), divided by len(truth_lines). Placing the full gold tree inside the tags gives 1.0 on that reward, even though a second, different tree follows it. The indentation check `line.startswith(' ') or line.rstrip() == answer_lines[0]` lets the second tree's root line through, because it equals the first line. Similarity ratio = 2*21/(32+21) ≈ 0.79. Total ≈ 0.3*0.79 + 0.7*1.0 ≈ 0.94.",
